<attribute name="background" nodeId="27133b73">&lt;p&gt;
    The project plan may be provided in both Microsoft Project and Excel formats. The preferred format is Microsoft Project
    as you will have the full facilities of Microsoft Project to tailor and level your plan. However, where Microsoft
    Project is not available or where the plan is relatively straightforward, Microsoft Excel may be an acceptable
    substitute for you. Milestones will show as zero hours and tasks will default to eight
    hours unless estimates have been included in the method content.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="goals" nodeId="e5d6242f">&lt;p&gt;
    Use this project plan as a starting point for the design&amp;nbsp;of an engagement and planning the delivery of this
    service. Remember that this project plan is only intended&amp;nbsp;as an initial draft that&amp;nbsp;indicates what you might
    do and will require further customization for your project. A prudent project manager will use a combination of the
    guidance contained in this method, his/her own experience, project planning skill, and the specific requirements of the
    project stakeholders in order to develop a suitable plan.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Download the project plan to view it in Microsoft Project.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        View the higher-level tasks by using the Outline function on the View panel. Viewing the plan at Outline Level 3
        will give a good high-level summary of the structure.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Go to the Resource Names column in the plan and filter by the role of your choice. This is an excellent way to see
        how the responsibilities of a particular role are distributed throughout the delivery process.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        For methods that have defined workstreams, you can also go to the workstream column in the plan and filter by the
        workstream of your choice. This is an excellent way to see how tasks from a particular workstream are distributed
        throughout the delivery process.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        View the Resource Sheet to see how the roles are distributed to each task in the method from the perspective of
        that role.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        On the Gantt Chart view, the leftmost column will have a hyperlink to the task in the method web represented by a
        small blue globe. Hold down the CTRL key and click that globe to bring up a context-sensitive task topic in your
        default browser.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
